Package: prspace
Title: Probability Spaces with the Same Syntax in R and Python
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: person("Ivan", "Gutierrez", email = "gutierrezi0222@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Write probability statements such as 'Pr[X == 0] <- 0.25' and
    read them back with 'Pr[X == 0]'. Events can declare their support
    (real, integer, count, or a finite set), and anything the rules of
    probability then pin down, such as complements and totals, is derived.
    Assignments that contradict earlier ones are flagged with the range of
    values that would have been consistent. A companion Python package on
    PyPI offers the same syntax.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
URL: https://github.com/ivanharvard/prspace
BugReports: https://github.com/ivanharvard/prspace/issues
